  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessment and Selection of Water Efficient Technologies for Textile Wet Processing Factories in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The fashion and textiles sector is among the most water-intensive industries globally, consuming an estimated 93 billion cubic meters annually and contributing around 20% of global wastewater.  Bangladesh, as the world&#x2019;s second-largest exporter of garments, faces a dual challenge: rising global scrutiny on supply chain sustainability and severe local water stress, with groundwater levels falling by up to three meters per year in some areas. Through a study the Resilient Water Accelerator seeks to advance sustainable water
management in Bangladesh&#x2019;s textile sector by assessing, validating, and scaling water-efficient technologies within priority clusters in Gazipur and Narayanganj.</narrative>
  </description>
